WEBVTT

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.940
Men, the MDC is facing a crisis!

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.520
<b>Mysterious Discovery Club</b>

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.520
At this rate, we won't be 
promoted to an official club.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.690
<b>Topic

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.650
Even though we announced our 
accomplishments of the past year

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.760
at the cultural festival the other day,

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.240
<b>Great Luvilca Exhibition</b>

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.240
<b>Reception</b>

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.240
only five people came.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.490
With that in mind,

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:23.460
we must think of ways to raise the 
visibility of the Mysterious Discovery Club.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.380
I know!

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.500
Do you have an idea, Tanako-kun?

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.500
Let's form a band!

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.630
What?

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:33.880
<b>High School Band Heaven</b>

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.880
Look at this!

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:37.550
High School Band Heaven?

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.160
Oh, that TV show that's on late at night?

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.050
Yes, that's it.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.460
This is nonsense.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.060
What good will participating in that do for us?

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:49.940
If you make it to the third round,

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.320
you get to appear on TV!

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.820
If we win, it's sure to raise our visibility!

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.230
Just imagine...

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:01.820
our band name being announced in grand style!

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.740
"The Mysterious Discovery Club!"

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.790
<b>The Mysterious Discovery Club!!</b>

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:11.800
<b>The Mysterious Discovery Club!</b>

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.080
Let's do it!

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:53.730
Girls' Band Formed

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.030
<b>Topic

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:10.370
We need a guitarist, bassist,
 drummer, and vocalist!

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:14.870
This may have been a bit too hard for us.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:17.510
That dream didn't last long.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.240
It's not over yet.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.840
I have an idea.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.770
Leave the gathering of members to me.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.020
I know that's what she said, but...

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.410
I don't think it's possible for Tanako-chan

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.200
to find members alone.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:40.320
Besides, if we're forming a band...

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.160
Yay!

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.250
Yay!

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.420
It should be like a dream!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.910
Don't you want it to be like a dream come true?!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.980
So, let's help her out!

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.710
For you, that was unusually passionate, Shibaraku.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:04.930
I don't want to see Tanako-chan depressed because

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:06.680
we couldn't find enough members.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.220
<b>MDC Recruiting Band Members!!</b>

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.770
<b>The Next Morning</b>

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:14.350
MDC band members!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.230
Take a recruitment flyer!

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.750
C'mon, let me see your English homework.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:19.870
No way!

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.580
Hey, will you go somewhere with me after school?

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.390
Where?

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.710
The café by the station.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.440
There's this really hot guy who works there.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.240
Seriously? Let's go!

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.940
Their cakes are supposed to be really good.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:38.850
Yeah?

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.640
They don't get it.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.050
If you want to reach out to people,

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.510
<b>Light Music Club</b>

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.510
this is the only place to do it.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:54.960
So you see, the MDC is forming a band.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:56.810
I recognize this.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.850
It's Band Heaven.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.130
This could be cool.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.280
It sounds fun.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:02.740
Should we enter?

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.320
What song should we play?

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.030
<i>Okay! It'll work!</i>

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:06.880
And...

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.820
You'll be wearing this!

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:08.820
<b>Bunny Girl Style!!</b>

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:08.820
Wow♥ Voluptuous! 
Hee hee!

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.540
Pervert!

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:16.540
Pervert?

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.830
Get out!

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.390
You pervert!

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:19.920
Hey!

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.430
I wasn't finished—

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:24.550
Perverted actions will not go unpunished!

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.890
N-No, I was just handing out these flyers.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.100
<b>Bunny Girl Style!!</b>

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.100
Wow♥ Voluptuous! 
Hee hee!

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.810
200 point penalty!

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:32.800
Huh?

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.890
Crap! This is the dream one!

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.330
Kyoko!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.680
<i>All that's left is...</i>

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.910
<b>Mysterious Discovery Club</b>

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.910
We tried recruiting members,

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.670
but no one came forward.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:05:59.860
Sniffle, sniffle...

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.000
I was naïve.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.140
I had no idea girls hated you so much, Shibaraku.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.880
We failed to gather members.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:11.430
We didn't fail.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.640
Tanako-chan!

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:14.720
Did you...

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.230
You found members?

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.730
Come on in, everyone.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.480
I don't know many boys,

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.240
so I ended up with more girls.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.020
First is our guitarist, Sawashita-san.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:34.380
I wanted to enter after seeing it on TV.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.620
<i>Sawashita-san, also known as "Moving Basketballs"!</i>

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:44.880
While we were at the hot springs, 
I heard she was taking guitar lessons.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.000
So I asked for her help, and she happily agreed.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.590
I look forward to working with you.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:55.190
Next is our bassist, Inoue-san.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:59.890
I was bitter about accidentally buying a bass 
instead of a guitar in middle school,

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.270
so I practiced out of stubbornness.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.400
That sounds like you, Inoue.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.390
Hey!

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.900
Who cares about that?

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:08.190
Well...

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:13.620
<b>Pose</b>

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.540
I'm not that interested in gaudy events, anyway.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.620
<i>She's raring to go!</i>

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:18.440
Our drummer is Inoue-san's friend, Izumi-san.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:22.890
No one has better timing or greater 
strength than this miraculous punchster.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.000
Hit...

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:30.500
I know this girl's strength better than anyone!

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:34.150
And I'm on the keyboard!

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:39.140
<i>We formed a girls' band?</i>

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.150
<i>Tanako-chan is amazing.</i>

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.310
<i>No wonder her planning skills, executive ability,</i>

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:47.030
<i>and quickness to assume are 
renowned as the highest in her class.</i>

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:49.210
I don't see a vocalist.

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.130
<i>That's right.</i>

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:52.960
<i>We don't have a vocalist.</i>

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:54.120
<i>Which means...</i>

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.900
<i>My dream is coming true!</i>

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.540
Our all-important vocalist is...

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.240
Rurumo-san!

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.160
What's a vocalist?

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.100
What's wrong, Shibaraku?

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.440
I happened to hear Rurumo-san singing

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:10.130
while I was walking behind the cafeteria.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.540
Her voice was so beautiful,

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.340
I thought it was worth a shot.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:18.220
Now, let everyone hear your voice!

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.280
Huh?

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:22.350
Shibaki-senpai, please ask your sister to sing for us!

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.150
Huh? Me?

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:28.360
<i>Come to think of it, 
I've never heard Rurumo sing before.</i>

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:34.520
Um, so, we'd like you to sing a song.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.410
A song?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.240
Don't worry.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.610
It can be something quick and simple.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.840
Can I sing a song of the spirit world?

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.600
Sure, go for it.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.800
She says she'll sing.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.880
<i>Mysteries of the ocean.</i>

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:57.090
<i>Mysteries of the sky.</i>

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:02.020
<i>Mysteries, mysteries.</i>

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.480
<i>La-la-la-la.</i>

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.040
I'm sorry.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.010
That's all I know.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.840
Singing is surprisingly embarrassing.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:17.820
I must return to work.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:22.160
<b>Moved!!</b>

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:22.160
<b>Ooh!!</b>

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:22.160
<b>Wow</b>

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:22.160
<b>Impressive!</b>

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:22.160
<b>Tears...</b>

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.400
Hold up!

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:20.170
That was great!

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:21.080
Impressive!

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.290
Amazing!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.790
<b>Music Room</b>

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.790
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:27.170
First, we should decide what you'll sing.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.750
It's not this kind of band.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.800
I added more lyrics to Rurumo-san's 
song from yesterday

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:37.280
and set it to a melody.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:39.140
Let me play it for you.

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:08.790
Yeah!

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.570
Let's keep working with that.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:12.290
Yeah.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.590
This is amazing.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.590
I'm so excited.

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:15.420
Yeah!

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.380
I think this will turn out great!

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.840
<b>Music Room</b>

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.840
<b>Another Day</b>

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.840
Next, we need lyrics.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:24.500
All right! I'll write some cool ones.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.520
I came up with some fantastic lyrics!

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.310
Huh?

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.100
<b>The Mysterious Discovery Song</b>

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.480
They really are fantastic.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.240
Not what I'd expect from 
a guy who looks like him.

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:36.070
What? It's exactly what I expected.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:36.780
Huh?

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:44.370
More beautiful than fragments of stars...

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:46.750
What are ya doin' this time?

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:50.960
I am something called a vocalist 
in a thing called a band.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.370
You've been doin' a lot of stuff like that lately.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:57.790
Well, as long as you're havin' fun.

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:07.780
<i>Do your best.</i>

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.940
<b>Music Room</b>

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.940
The next thing we need is costumes!

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.070
<b>Bunny Girl Style!!</b>

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.070
Wow♥ Voluptuous! 
Hee hee!

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.070
It's gotta be these!

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:17.790
Nope!

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.030
My man's dream!

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:23.230
My man's dream...

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:24.930
By the way,

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:27.610
what do you think of wearing matching outfits?

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:29.110
Good idea.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:30.600
What should we wear?

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:31.830
Excuse me...

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.280
Oh, Masako.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:36.960
Actually, about your outfits...

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.470
How do you feel about 
Ruru-chan's witch's costume?

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:44.450
I think it would match the image of the MDC.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:45.820
Good idea!

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:46.760
You're right.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:49.260
Nice idea, Senpai.

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:50.930
Let's do it, Shimomura-san.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.080
It would be cute with ribbons.

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.290
You're right.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:59.030
But isn't that kind of outfit expensive?

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.030
Masako can make them.

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:02.280
What?

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.820
Masako is skilled at making clothes.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:13.920
Seeing you all work so hard made me want to help.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.040
If there's anything I can do, let me know.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.540
<b>Wardrobe Room</b>

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.630
We do this here...

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:24.220
I had no idea Masako was good at making clothes.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.820
She's just like a professional.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:29.500
I'd even ask her to make normal clothes for me.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:30.220
Right?

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.980
How did you do this part?

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.690
This is gorgeous!

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.290
Hey, everyone!

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:37.230
We got this notice in the club room.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:40.410
The first round of judging is this Sunday.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:41.990
It's nearly time.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.740
Let's do our best, everyone!

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.990
Yeah!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.040
<b>Making a banner to show their support on TV</b>

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.040
<b>Pull</b>

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.040
<b>Poke Poke</b>

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.040
<b>Sew Sew</b>

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:52.620
Next, please.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:56.330
<b>High School 
Band Heaven
First Round Judging</b>

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:56.330
Number 36, the Mysterious Discovery Club.

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:01.420
<i>Oh, they're witches.</i>

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.800
<i>A cosplay band, huh?</i>

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.380
<i>These are always so...</i>

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:17.110
Sing into this thing, okay?

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:18.520
Got it.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:24.490
<i>They just formed recently and 
decided they had to audition, huh?</i>

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:29.240
<i>This year's Band Heaven harvest is pretty poor.</i>

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.320
Okay, here we go.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:48.080
<i>Mysteries of the ocean.</i>

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:52.260
<i>Mysteries of the sky.</i>

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:56.940
<i>Mysteries, mysteries.</i>

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:00.860
<i>La-la-la-la.</i>

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:17.160
<i>Let's gather all the mysteries</i>

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:26.170
<i>And create a necklace</i>

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:40.650
<i>More beautiful than fragments of stars.</i>

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:52.990
N...

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:57.290
Number 36, the Mysterious Discovery Club, passes!

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:58.770
We did it!

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.400
All right!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:05.050
<b>High School
 LOVE MUSIC 
Band Heaven</b>

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:05.050
<b>Second Round Judging</b>

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:05.050
The Mysterious Discovery Club passes 
the second round of judging!

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.000
<b>PASS</b>

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:07.480
Of course we did.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:08.970
That's great.

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:10.470
We did it!

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:11.930
You!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.670
You have the voice of an angel.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.700
I'm expecting good things 
from you in the final round.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.850
Cheers!

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:23.360
Man, this is great.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.400
Well, we practiced.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.930
Still, you look pretty happy about it.

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:30.040
I'm so glad we made it, though.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:33.240
But their praise was focused on the prodigy girl.

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:35.950
"You have the voice of an angel."

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:38.780
"I'm expecting good things 
from you in the final round."

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:41.360
That's what the guy in the glasses said.

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:43.710
I bet we're gonna win this! Right?

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.090
We will win!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.170
Whoa! Inoue's serious!

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.220
Right, Ruru-chan?

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:51.170
Huh?

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:53.800
"Chan"? What's gotten into you?

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.230
That's what Masako calls her. Right?

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:57.390
Y-Yeah.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.180
Can I call you Ruru-chan, too?

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.140
Yes.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.860
There's something I want to ask you, Ruru-san.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.070
What is it?

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:10.370
I forced you to join the band,

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.690
but are you having fun?

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:17.560
I'm glad we're in a band together, personally.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.330
Me, too.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.540
I'm having fun, too.

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:27.280
Oh, good.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:28.450
Ruru-san...

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:31.590
I mean, Ruru-chan, I'm glad you're having fun.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:35.470
Okay, let's play through the song one more time!

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.240
Yeah!

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:38.790
Let us help you prepare, for the sake of the MDC!

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.090
Yeah!

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:42.560
As long as we're doing this, let's win!

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:46.220
It's great that you made friends with everyone.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:48.190
Why are you so happy?

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.020
Huh?

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:51.610
Um... Am I?

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:54.450
You seem to be in higher spirits than usual.

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:56.090
Really?

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:01.570
I guess that's because you can't ride a broom.

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:05.250
You're not athletic, and your instincts are poor.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.580
You can't lie, either.

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:10.340
But you're actually good at singing.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.920
People recognize there's something you do well.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.460
Of course it makes me happy.

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:18.350
We've been together for a while.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:21.350
I guess it matters to me, too.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.710
<i>Happy?</i>

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:26.060
<i>For me?</i>

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:32.640
Does that make you happy, too?

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:38.440
No, that was just a reflexive, uh...

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:43.580
Whether or not you are happy 
is not my concern.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.080
Let's get started, Ruru-chan.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.960
Yes. Let's do it.

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:54.920
Ruru-san!

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:57.010
We heard from Shiba.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:18:00.000
The final round is this Sunday.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.010
We'll go to support you.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:03.520
Thank you.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.800
I'd march through a storm 
to support you, Ruru-san!

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:06.790
We'll be there!

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:07.940
Do your best.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:12.230
<b>High School Band Heaven 
Final Round</b>

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:14.980
I've always wanted to see this live.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:14.980
<b>Grasp victory!!
Tarantula ver. 2.5</b>

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:17.000
We're finally here.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.160
Let's do our best.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:18.630
Yes.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:19.510
Yeah.

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:20.800
What is this?

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:22.920
This is where the final round's taking place.

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:24.240
Look. Can you see it?

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:26.440
That bright place over there.

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:28.000
You'll be doing it there.

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:29.520
Doing what?

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:30.790
Singing.

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:32.020
Who?

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:33.500
You.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.640
Are you okay, Ruru-chan?

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.160
Ruru-chan!

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.160
Rurumo! Hey, Rurumo!

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:44.100
Are you okay?

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:46.020
Shibaki, you must have...

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.230
I didn't do anything!

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:50.750
This has been Stealth Seven!

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.400
Let's give them a hand!

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.940
What should we do? We're up soon.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:58.620
I-I'm okay.

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:00.160
Don't force yourself.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.610
You're shaking. Do you have a cold?

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.470
<i>Damn it. I hadn't even considered this.</i>

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.580
<i>Why isn't it in a studio,
 like it has been until now?</i>

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:10.460
<i>Rurumo can't sing in front of a crowd.</i>

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:14.380
<i>She's a lot more shy than most people!</i>

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.130
I'm okay.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:22.760
Don't worry about me.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:25.790
Let's go.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.180
<b>Ruru-san LOVE</b>

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:31.720
The name of the MDC will 
finally reach the entire nation.

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:34.340
We haven't done anything, though...

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:38.740
But her voice is so beautiful, 
I want everyone to hear it.

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:41.040
It's finally time, President.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:44.090
This next band is your favorite, is it?

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:44.980
Yes.

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:47.040
They're sure to be a huge hit.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.000
Hey, Rurumo!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.790
It's... okay.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.500
I'll... sing.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.640
I'll do it.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:00.220
That is your wish, isn't it?

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:01.930
<i>Rurumo...</i>

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:10.880
Appearing on the final round stage next is

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:13.740
the voice of an angel who appeared like a comet!

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:17.940
The miraculous girls' band, 
the Mysterious Discovery Club!

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.650
Their song is "The Mysterious Discovery Song"!

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:27.730
What is that?

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.200
Their vocalist is a guy.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.160
<i>It's no surprise.</i>

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.920
<i>She's so shy, she'd rather go to prison</i>

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.350
<i>than put on panties in front of someone.</i>

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:40.380
<i>And yet, I...</i>

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:45.340
<i>I won't let your hard work go to waste!</i>

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:50.060
Listen to the shout of our souls!

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:54.690
<i>Mysteries of the ocean.</i>

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:58.520
<i>Mysteries of the sky.</i>

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:02.820
<b><i>Groan</i></b>

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:03.650
<i>Mysteries, mysteries.</i>

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:07.240
<i>La-la-la-la.</i>

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.240
A huge hit, huh?

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:11.260
The MDC was terrible.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:16.660
Well, we made some nice memories.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:19.380
It's amazing that we made it to the final round.

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:22.340
<i>I'm... tone-deaf...</i>

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.080
Don't feel bad.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:29.340
Everyone has something they cannot do.

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:31.800
Yeah, you're one to talk!

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:33.150
You tried your hardest.

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:34.260
Of course I did!

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:36.370
I sang the best I could!

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:38.900
When you realized I couldn't sing,

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.400
you did your best for me.

00:21:42.850 --> 00:21:44.360
The moon is nice tonight.

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.650
To thank you,

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:48.600
I will sing for you later.

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:05.680
<i>Mysteries of the water.</i>

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:10.200
<i>Mysteries of the earth.</i>

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:14.680
<i>Mysteries, mysteries.</i>

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:19.150
<i>La-la-la-la.</i>

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:34.440
<i>Let's search for all the everyday mysteries</i>

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:44.000
<i>And create a jewel</i>

00:22:44.000 --> 00:23:00.120
<i>That shines brighter than the light of the moon.</i>

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:09.780
<i>This reminds me...</i>

00:23:10.440 --> 00:23:13.250
<i>of the first time we met.</i>

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:16.530
<i>It's almost winter, huh?</i>

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:18.910
<i>Time flies...</i>

00:23:30.490 --> 00:23:32.010
"A Day Without Rurumo."

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Next Episode: A Day Without Rurumo</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Illustration by Iizuka Haruko</b>
